{"title":"Kim Tschang-Yeul, Water Drops","link":"https://kottke.org/26/09/kim-tschang-yeul-water-drops","date":1790716200000,"content":"\n         \t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672269-eac1e18f.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672269-eac1e18f.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672269-eac1e18f.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672283-74649755.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672283-74649755.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672283-74649755.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672295-4eb8b8b6.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672295-4eb8b8b6.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672295-4eb8b8b6.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672300-2cda0c76.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672300-2cda0c76.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1790672300-2cda0c76.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>From the early 1970s until his death in 2021, Korean artist Kim Tschang-Yeul painted water droplets. From <a href=\"https://www.alminerech.com/artists/7456-kim-tschang-yeul\">one of the galleries</a> representing his work:</p>\n\t<blockquote><p>The waterdrop was the starting point for a singular and iconic body of work, which stands at the confluence of lyrical abstraction, Pop art and Chinese calligraphy. This simple and limpid œuvre subtly fuses Taoist wisdom, modern conceptual irony and the tragedy of war.</p></blockquote>\n\t<p>You can view more of Kim’s work at <a href=\"https://www.thisiscolossal.com/2021/02/kim-tschang-yeul-water-drops\">Colossal</a> and <a href=\"https://theinspirationgrid.com/water-drops-paintings-by-kim-tschang-yeul\">InspirationGrid</a>.\n</p>\n \n\n        \n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Kim%20Tschang-Yeul\">Kim Tschang-Yeul</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/water\">water</a></p>\n        \n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"533daac6e611fed6cc67a927669fb250892590ec11d2ed5de1ddfd113f1d8b7c","category":"Sites"}